{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788116215,"nonce":"UF2HLJ+ckymufzG2IYXDo99HRWU=","message":"AMENDMENT from spike 0.1 (FINDINGS.md, git-bug 3fa4cf5) — orchestrator, post-gate.\n\nTwo bench facts this spec can rely on. Scope and Acceptance stand.\n\n**devMode is already on.** `profile/make-profile-agent.sh` seeds\n`devMode=True` in the bench Prefs.xml, so the DebugActions catalog this spec\nwraps is available without any per-run arrangement. (It is also why the bench\nlogs six benign `StaticConstructorOnStartup` hygiene warnings every boot — that\nreport is dev-mode-gated. Triaged in FINDINGS section 5; not this spec's\nproblem.)\n\n**There is a no-UI path into a fixture, which is what `dev:starter-kit` is\nultimately for.** With devMode on, a save named `autostart.rws` in the bench\nSaves dir is loaded automatically on entering the Play scene\n(`SaveGameFilesUtility.GetAutostartSaveFile`); `Root_Play.Start` also honors\n`Find.GameInitData.gameToLoad`. Either beats `-quicktest`, which regenerates a\nworld every boot (2-4 min) and hands you Cassandra **Rough** whether you wanted\nher or not. Worth designing the starter-kit config format so its output can be\nsaved as such a fixture.\n\n**Journaled-as-cheat has a consumer already.** The spike confirmed the bench\nruns with `pauseOnError=False` and `automaticPauseMode=Never` — the mod owns\ntime end to end — so a `dev:incident` raid will run straight into whatever\n`advance` is doing. The `dev` journal event this spec must write is what makes\nthat legible after the fact; it is the only provenance there will be.","files":null}]}